# Announcing oo2c 2.2.4: a revived fork of the Optimizing Oberon-2 Compiler

This software was developed with the aid of AI.

oo2c, the Optimizing Oberon-2 Compiler from the OOC project, translates Oberon-2 to C. Its development stopped in 2011, and its last release no longer builds on current systems. My fork brings it back: 2.2.4 builds, runs and passes its tests on Linux (x86-64, aarch64 and i386), on FreeBSD, and on OpenBSD and NetBSD in both 32-bit and 64-bit, and the generated C compiles with gcc 16 with no warnings. A release tarball bootstraps with no oo2c installed.

